  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S={2,5,11}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $6$ cards labeled with two, $6$ cards labeled with five, and $8$ cards labeled with eleven (twenty cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2) & =\\frac{6}{20}=\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ P(5) & =\\frac{6}{20}=\\frac{3}{10} \\\\ P(11) & =\\frac{8}{20}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =2\\cdot f(2)+5\\cdot f(5)+11\\cdot f(11) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3}{10})+5(\\frac{3}{10})+11(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{15}{10}+\\frac{22}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{15}{10}+\\frac{44}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{6+15+44}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{65}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
